import json,statistics as st,html,sys,collections,math
from pathlib import Path
p=Path(sys.argv[1]);rows=[json.loads(s) for s in (p/'games.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()];assert len(rows)==60
mean=lambda a:round(st.mean(a),2) if a else None
q=lambda a,f:sorted(a)[min(len(a)-1,int(f*len(a)))] if a else None
summary=[]
for n in [None,2,3,4]:
 for policy in [None,'self','mixed']:
  a=[r for r in rows if (n is None or r['players']==n) and (policy is None or r['cohort']==policy)];f=[r for r in a if r.get('endReason')=='finish'];prices=[x for r in a for x in r.get('prices',[])];actions=[r['actions'] for r in f]
  summary.append(dict(players=n or 'all',policy=policy or 'all',games=len(a),finished=len(f),censored=sum(r['status']=='censored' for r in a),failed=sum(r['status']=='failed' for r in a),gap=mean([r['range'] for r in f]),third=mean([r['thirdLag'] for r in f]),actionsMean=mean(actions),actionsMedian=st.median(actions) if actions else None,actionsP90=q(actions,.9),auctionMean=mean(prices),auctionMedian=st.median(prices) if prices else None,auctionP90=q(prices,.9)))
finish=[r for r in rows if r.get('endReason')=='finish'];usage={t:mean([r['types'][t] for r in finish]) for t in ['call','valueAction','changeFounder','raiseMoney']};values=collections.Counter(v for r in rows for v in r.get('values',[]));founders={}
for r in rows:
 for fid,v in r.get('founderMovement',{}).items():
  a=founders.setdefault(fid,{'founder':fid,'gamesWithMovement':0,'forward':0,'backward':0});a['gamesWithMovement']+=1;a['forward']+=v.get('forward',0);a['backward']+=v.get('backward',0)
metrics={'summary':summary,'completedActionMeans':usage,'cutoffs':dict(collections.Counter(r.get('cutoff') for r in rows if r['status']=='censored')),'valuePlays':dict(values),'founderMovement':list(founders.values())};(p/'metrics.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2));print(json.dumps(metrics['summary'][0]));
if not (p/'sample-review.json').exists():sys.exit()
reviews=json.loads((p/'sample-review.json').read_text());attempts=json.loads((p/'sample-index.json').read_text());manifest=json.loads((p/'manifest.json').read_text());complete=[r for r in attempts if r['status']=='complete'];a=summary[0]
esc=html.escape
def table(rs,keys):return '<table><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+esc(k)+'</th>' for k in keys)+'</tr>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+esc(str(r[k]) if r.get(k) is not None else '—')+'</td>' for k in keys)+'</tr>' for r in rs)+'</table>'
body=f'<h1>v137 · Only fundraising spends deal-flow</h1><p>Nine cards/company · five starting cards · draw three at leg end · run-01</p><p><b>{a["finished"]}/60 reached 24; {a["censored"]}/60 unfinished at the research cutoff; {a["failed"]} errors.</b> Non-funding actions preserve the hand, including when empty. Public value effects can issue shares without a matching deal-flow card. The tabletop retains its existing layout.</p>'
body+='<h2>The result</h2>'+table([r for r in summary if r['policy']=='all'],['players','games','finished','censored','gap','third','actionsMedian','actionsP90'])
body+='<p>Gap is first minus last; third is first minus third. Spread and action duration above include only games reaching24, so survivor selection matters. Actions count turns, not bids, acknowledgements or human minutes. Provisional targets remain ≥95% completion, mean gap≤16 and third≤8; these are design hypotheses, not user-specified thresholds.</p>'
body+='<p>The empty-hand rules deadlock is removed. The remaining obstruction is bot behavior: raising capital adds cash and an equal exit liability, so it changes liquidity but not net score. Bots can repeatedly reject investments and call capital. The study stops after twelve consecutive capital-only rounds, or 2,000 commands. These are research cutoffs, not new game-ending rules. A separate smoke game at seed8101 with four balanced players also failed to end after2,000 commands.</p><p>Funding scarcity now applies only to ordinary matching-card calls. Rights Issue, Convertible Notes, Tender Offer and Sweat Equity can create shares through public values without consuming that company’s deal-flow supply. This is a consequence of the requested rule, not a separate exception added to the engine. Value-driven movement and explicit founder reactions also bypass ordinary fundraising scarcity.</p>'
body+='<h2>Comparison and limitations</h2><p>v136 reached24 in3/60 games and stalled in57/60 because all hands emptied. Matched seeds and lineups are retained, but v137 uses the additional capital-loop research cutoff. Its unfinished games cannot be called permanent stalls or losses. Bot bidding/scoring is unchanged; the bot revision only removes support-action discard fields and handles empty hands. This is evidence about these policies, not optimal human play.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>Policy breakdown and auction prices</summary>'+table([r for r in summary if r['policy']!='all'],['players','policy','games','finished','censored','gap','third','actionsMean','auctionMean','auctionMedian','auctionP90'])+'<p>Prices include sold auctions from all attempted games, including unfinished games.</p></details>'
body+='<details><summary>Actions and components</summary><p>Mean action usage in completed games:</p>'+table([usage],list(usage))+'<p>Value plays across all attempted games; raw counts, not exposure-normalized strength rankings:</p>'+table([{'value':k,'plays':v} for k,v in values.most_common()],['value','plays'])+'<p>Founder-triggered movement ledger totals across all attempted games. Attribution can overlap and is not a causal strength estimate. gamesWithMovement counts games with a ledger entry, not all market exposure.</p>'+table(list(founders.values()),['founder','gamesWithMovement','forward','backward'])+'</details>'
supplement=json.loads((p/'supplement-index.json').read_text());suppComplete=[r for r in supplement if r['status']=='complete']
body+=f'<h2>Ten completed replay reviews</h2><p>The original ten fixed slots produced {len(complete)} completed games in {len(attempts)} attempts. A separately recorded supplemental protocol selected the first five completed mixed-policy games from seeds9401 upward, rotating player counts; {len(supplement)} attempts produced {len(suppComplete)} completions. All attempts are retained and replay-verified. Supplemental games are not pooled into the primary statistics. This selection overrepresents mixed policies and survivors; it does not establish healthy balance. Ten completed traces and one unfinished diagnostic are reviewed below.</p><p><a href="supplement-protocol.json">Supplemental selection protocol</a> · <a href="supplement-index.json">All supplemental attempts</a></p>'
for r in reviews:
 seed=r['seed'];body+=f'<details><summary>Sample {seed}</summary><p>{esc(r["review"])}</p><a href="samples/{seed}.json">Full trace and decisions</a> · <a href="samples/{seed}-replay.json">Importable replay</a></details>'
body+='<h2>Next experiment</h2><p>Keep this rule set fixed and separately fix the bot’s repeated capital fallback and longer-term investment valuation. Then compare policies on matched seeds before interpreting spread as a rules-only outcome. No extra refill, forced investment or automatic settlement was added.</p>'
body+='<details><summary>Reproduce and audit</summary><p>Frozen source '+esc(manifest['source'])+'</p><p><a href="manifest.json">Protocol</a> · <a href="metrics.json">Metrics</a> · <a href="games.jsonl">Primary games</a> · <a href="sample-index.json">Sample attempts</a> · <a href="runtime.json">Runtime</a> · <a href="source/scripts/mild-dice-study.js">Frozen runner</a></p><pre>node scripts/mild-dice-study.js NEW_DIRECTORY\npython3 scripts/funding-dice-report.py NEW_DIRECTORY</pre><p>Renderer requires authored sample-review.json. All rules and bot source was frozen before the cohort. No cutoffs are counted as completed games.</p></details>'
(p/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>v137 funding-card study</title><style>body{font:17px/1.55 system-ui;max-width:1060px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;background:#f8f6ef;color:#243029}h1{line-height:1.2}table{border-collapse:collapse;display:block;overflow:auto;font-size:14px}td,th{padding:8px;border-bottom:1px solid #ccc;text-align:left}details{margin:18px 0;padding:16px;background:white;border:1px solid #ccc;border-radius:8px}summary{font-weight:bold;cursor:pointer}a{color:#17624a}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere}</style>'+body+'</html>')
